{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205615-orpheus","id":205615,"title":"Orpheus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-22T20:53:45-07:00","id":205615,"title":"Orpheus","content":"I know this has already been asked. If there is a link or something, please hook me up. So, anyone crossed Orpheus with Geist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","user":"ChewyGranola","date":". 07-22-2014, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T23:18:29-07:00","id":205767,"title":"","content":"Project Orpheus gets a reference in Book of the Dead, some sin-eaters looking for the ghosts of celebrities ran into &quot;alive and dead at the same time&quot; ghosts in black.<br /> <br /> Some people have worked on adding orpheus to geist on this forum or the old one, if not both, although for my money I'd make Orpheus hunters.<br /> <br /> Also, the men in black folks at Valkyrie have suits that allow them to enter other dimensions, including the underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T01:52:09-07:00","id":205827,"title":"","content":"Yeah I saw that in Book of the Dead. It was cool.<br /> <br /> I totally see Orpheus as a group of hunters. I also think it would be fun to have a Krewe incorporate, maybe even evolving to Tier 2 with time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T06:37:05-07:00","id":206011,"title":"","content":"I see Orpheus as a Hunter Conspiracy, featuring a Projection Endowment. I\u2019d see it as a highly customizable Endowment, in a manner similar to how things like pre-GMC \u201csafe places\u201d were modeled: multiple aspects representing different facets of the Projection, such as what you need to do to Project (ranging from \u201centomb yourself in a technological coffin and let a machine induce clinical death for the duration of your Projection\u201d to \u201csit quietly in a (hopefully) secure location of your choosing and meditate\u201d), how long you can maintain the projection before your life is endangered, what Numina and Manifestations you have access to while Projected, and what Rank you have as a ghost. I\u2019d handle this in a manner similar to how the Blood Bathing Ritual is handled in <b>Immortals</b>; but instead of the total of the various features being zero, they\u2019d be however many dots you\u2019ve invested into the Projection Endowment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-23-2014, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T10:16:04-07:00","id":206274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205615-orpheus?p=206011#post206011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see Orpheus as a Hunter Conspiracy, featuring a Projection Endowment. I\u2019d see it as a highly customizable Endowment, in a manner similar to how things like pre-GMC \u201csafe places\u201d were modeled: multiple aspects representing different facets of the Projection, such as what you need to do to Project (ranging from \u201centomb yourself in a technological coffin and let a machine induce clinical death for the duration of your Projection\u201d to \u201csit quietly in a (hopefully) secure location of your choosing and meditate\u201d), how long you can maintain the projection before your life is endangered, what Numina and Manifestations you have access to while Projected, and what Rank you have as a ghost. I\u2019d handle this in a manner similar to how the Blood Bathing Ritual is handled in <b>Immortals</b>; but instead of the total of the various features being zero, they\u2019d be however many dots you\u2019ve invested into the Projection Endowment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would make Orpheus a really good antagonist! I have found that Geist lacks a true antagonist, so maybe Orpheus fits the bill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T12:25:20-07:00","id":206434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205615-orpheus?p=206011#post206011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see Orpheus as a Hunter Conspiracy, featuring a Projection Endowment. I\u2019d see it as a highly customizable Endowment, in a manner similar to how things like pre-GMC \u201csafe places\u201d were modeled: multiple aspects representing different facets of the Projection, such as what you need to do to Project (ranging from \u201centomb yourself in a technological coffin and let a machine induce clinical death for the duration of your Projection\u201d to \u201csit quietly in a (hopefully) secure location of your choosing and meditate\u201d), how long you can maintain the projection before your life is endangered, what Numina and Manifestations you have access to while Projected, and what Rank you have as a ghost. I\u2019d handle this in a manner similar to how the Blood Bathing Ritual is handled in <b>Immortals</b>; but instead of the total of the various features being zero, they\u2019d be however many dots you\u2019ve invested into the Projection Endowment.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Awesome! Want to collaborate?<br /> <br /> Personally I'd like to say you're not a ghost but a psychic projection - That would be a nasty shock for Sin-Eaters when a lot of their cool powers don't work on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T12:27:14-07:00","id":206437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205615-orpheus?p=206434#post206434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... Awesome! Want to collaborate?<br /> <br /> Personally I'd like to say you're not a ghost but a psychic projection - That would be a nasty shock for Sin-Eaters when a lot of their cool powers don't work on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use Auspex 5 as inspiration, but for the Orpheus folks, it operates on the same frequency of Twilight as Ghosts. They could also get further powers based on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T14:01:48-07:00","id":206511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205615-orpheus?p=206274#post206274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would make Orpheus a really good antagonist! I have found that Geist lacks a true antagonist, so maybe Orpheus fits the bill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd consider the Orpheus Group's rivals, NextWorld and Terrel and Squib as better antagonists than Orpheus and Lazarus Redux. Or Wrath: the Oblivion's Orphic Circle. Or a group with similar aims to the Giovanni Clan. Canonically while Orpheus has done a number of morally questionable activities they aren't actively evil or being run by particularly evil individuals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T14:08:59-07:00","id":206518,"title":"","content":"That works in their favour though.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters vs Orpheus isn't a tale of good vs evil. It's a tale of independent master artisans competing with mass production. Given the strong working class street-culture feel of the Bound that works quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T14:29:11-07:00","id":206564,"title":"","content":"@King's Raven:<br /> Which powers exactly? Cause obviously immunity to ones like the Stigmata marionette is a given, but I have a hard time justifying certain others like the Phantasmal Marionette. Then there is those powers that have a that vague statement of ephemeral beings and not Ghosts, or those two warding Ceremonies, or that one that turns objects into ephemeral things.<br /> <br /> Or maybe i'm completely misunderstanding what you mean by psychic projection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T10:19:52-07:00","id":207297,"title":"","content":"Generally I'm talking about Stigmata powers. So the Stigmata Boneyard won't be able to ward against you. The Stigmata Shroud doesn't increase Resistance against your powers or affect you with the two or three dot powers. Also Ceremonies like Warding Circle. Basically, anything that specifically says &quot;Ghost&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T12:27:53-07:00","id":207408,"title":"","content":"Okay, now in the underworld everything is physical and so the ghost description no longer matters because they also count all the other Manifestations that work on human targets, would they still work or is the Orpheus group in the Underworld right screwed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T12:40:35-07:00","id":207418,"title":"","content":"Where does it say that in the books? I don't remember anything saying that, e.g., the Stigmata Marionette will affect humans in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T14:30:42-07:00","id":207530,"title":"","content":"I mean that ephemeral beings are now pretty much physical in the Underworld and so this psychic manifestation thingy Orpheus has would pretty much be vulnerable to the other manifestations that didn't work on ghosts because they were incorporeal in twilight on the surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T00:50:14-07:00","id":207984,"title":"","content":"In witchfinders, there is a witch mystery that one can buy as a fifth level merit through gifted to be able to project as a ghost, fyi.<br /> <br /> So there are already people in nwod that are part time ghosts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T18:54:45-07:00","id":213026,"title":"","content":"Or you could turn Orpheus group into a krewe. That would do stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T09:24:44-07:00","id":213650,"title":"","content":"How about this for the Orpheus Project:<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Sometime in the mid 17th century, with science and occultism existing in tandem, a group of German and French occult scientists and Alchemists were working tirelessly to marry the abstract concepts of newly developing science with the ancient rites of occultism and kabbalism. As time went on, and their work yet bore little fruit, members of this occult society started to grow impatient and frustrated with their lack of sucess. Each apparent clue lead them to the grave of a person who might've answeres they were seeking, if not for the fact that they died decades if not centuries ago. The groups efforts took an almost archaeological and historical tune, as they spend weeks and months trying to piece together forgotten knowledge of dead occultists and Alchemists, in search of a knowledge they were certain the long dead possessed. As time went on, some members aged terribly and other simply dropped off the project for lack of progress.<br /> Sometime in the late 17th century, the group recieved a package from an anonymous source, with the symbol of Metatrons Cube as the insignia seal of the large package.<br /> Inside, they found a letter, a map, blueprints, multiple long slender hollow rods ending in a long thin spike and a strange hedronically shaped device made from a queer dark metal unlike anything they had before seen, with openings in which tubes could be inserted. The letter spoke of a realm beneath the earth harboring rivers of eternal life, where the shades of the dead may still linger. The letter went on to explain the nature of the rods and the hedronic device, refering to the latter as a Hex-Core, to be inserted into what the letter described as The Avernian Engine. By this profane device, the letter said that the knowledge of the dead could be extracted to be readily drunk by whoever wished. The blueprints in the package explained in full detail how to construct this Avernian Engine, placing the Hex-Core within it. All the device needed were the fuel; A shade to be extracted from, and the water from this River of Life to act as the catalyst. The letter, signed by a Mr Jambres, explained that the map showed the location of a gateway into the stygian realms located in South Germany, from which this river was readily accessible. It explain to them the nature of the rods, which could suposedly trap ghosts within them, if thrust into the shades while they were material, something Mr Jambres promised would be a given in the bleak realm in which the river lie. Out of desperation and a sense of awe at the strange device, the group decided to heed this advice and pursue their goal through the shadowy portal they found, after construction of the Engine was complete.<br /> What the letter failed to mention was the saw-toothed, faceless horror with multi-bifurcated veiny arms and quasi-humanoid body that guarded it.<br /> <br /> As the remnants of the group made their narrow escape from the skittering horror and back onto the surface world, they clutched mightily their stolen price; Water needed to fuel the Avernian Engine.<br /> They had been in luck during their jaunt into the Underworld. They had found a shade that one of the historically inclined members recognised as a major-general of an old German-Roman army, and so they had chosen his ghostly form to experiment on.<br /> The Scientists found that the essence of the dead could grant them much more than merely the knowledge that Mr Jambres had promised them. Their shadowy nature coursed through the occultists and mixed with the water from The River Of Life, which Mr Jambres refered to as Anahita, gave them a renewed sense of vigor.<br /> The only true downside to this concoction however, was that they could no longer sneak about as living in the Great Below as long they were under the effects of their elixir. Here, the shadowy nature of what they had stolen was readily visible to all, and they were seen as abominable mixes between living and dead. Wandering through the planes of death became impossible, as all the deathless guardian horrors that lurked there saw them for the crime they had committed, and chased them relentlessly out of the shadowry domain.<br /> Eventually, the group recruited new members to plunder the Great Dark for knowledgeable shades and additional water, even as the exlir's warded death away from the original members.<br /> <br /> These days, the group has expanded heavily and branched out. The halls of their headquarters, build atop the black gate that Mr Jambres map originally pointed to, is filled with the trapped shades of hundreds - if not thousands - of historical figures, which the inner circle sups on monthly to extend their unatural life and increase their stolen knowledge. The group deploys two departments of field agents, one group who ventures into the Avernian Dominions to gather more water and opduct more shades, and another which uses the stolen powers of the dead to convince would-be interlopers and inquisitive people to look the other way.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Whef. That became a bit more extensive than I had innitially imagined. Anyway. Let me know what you think. Will probably do something with this for my own Geist game, eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1958,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","user":"Krobeles","date":". 07-30-2014, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T20:15:43-07:00","id":214243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205615-orpheus?p=206434#post206434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... Awesome! Want to collaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot to subscribe to this thread, so I only just saw this. I wouldn\u2019t mind collaborating; but I suspect that there\u2019d be a lot of creative differences. For instance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205615-orpheus?p=206434#post206434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'd like to say you're not a ghost but a psychic projection - That would be a nasty shock for Sin-Eaters when a lot of their cool powers don't work on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d prefer the projection to be as ghost-like as possible, albeit inherently \u201cLucid Dead\u201d rather than the default three-attributes-and-one-track-mind ghosts featured in GMC. That said, I have no problem with the notion that the Lucid Dead are particularly resistant toSin-Eater powers (due to the whole \u201cfree will\u201d thing), and that Projectors are immune due to being living people having out-of-body experiences rather than actually being dead. But the ghost-form upgrades? Ghostly Numina and Manifestations. That\u2019s both to conserve word count and to emphasize how easy it is to mistake them for ghosts. I\u2019ll review the rest of this thread now\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T21:38:38-07:00","id":214367,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><u>Krobeles:</u> that\u2019s an intriguing antagonist group for Geist; but I wouldn\u2019t go with \u201cOrpheus\u201d as its name. I <i>would</i> like to see this done, and in the same vein as <b>Demon</b>\u2019s Deva Corp or <b>Mummy</b>\u2019s Last Dynasty International; just go with some other name than Orpheus.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><u>FallenEco:</u> I\u2019m sure something could be done with a corporate Sin-Eater krewe; but again, it\u2019s not something that says \u201cOrpheus\u201d to me. It <i>does</i> say \u201ctier three krewe\u201d, though.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><u>StSword:</u> true enough. Again, not \u201cOrpheus\u201d; but as you say, there\u2019s already precedent for part-time ghosts.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">To me, \u201cOrpheus\u201d needs to be a corporation that seeks to turn a profit by collaborating with ghosts; and it has technologies to empower its agents to interact with ghosts via projection. It ought to be presentable as a patron for protagonists, so it can\u2019t be <i>too</i> overtly exploitative; but as with any <b>Hunter</b> org, it ought to have a dark side that allows it to be suitable as an antagonist as well. So shades of potential exploitation are reasonable \u2014 just don\u2019t make them overt or their primary mode of operation.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T06:42:37-07:00","id":214607,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I was just going off of the referance in Book Of The Dead. I haven't really read Wraith or Orpheus, and I can understand you want to model them more on that? I just read the Whitewolf Wikia articles, and they both seem pretty cool. I dont quite see why you couldn't simply lift Orpheus directly though? A shadowy corporation that uses projection and ghost allies to its advantage, seems like an easy thing to set up?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T10:29:10-07:00","id":219252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205615-orpheus?p=214607#post214607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. I was just going off of the referance in Book Of The Dead. I haven't really read Wraith or Orpheus, and I can understand you want to model them more on that? I just read the Whitewolf Wikia articles, and they both seem pretty cool. I dont quite see why you couldn't simply lift Orpheus directly though? A shadowy corporation that uses projection and ghost allies to its advantage, seems like an easy thing to set up?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was me, yeah I would just lift the Orpheus Group largely as they are in OWoD and transplant them in the NWoD. They have everything to make for an excellent organization regardless of which world they exist in. And as I've mentioned, <i>Orpheus</i> already has two sinister rival companies that can easily be transplanted as well.<br /> <br /> But if you really are going to do that you kind of need some of the <i>Orpheus </i>books as there's plenty there that isn't talked about in in the White Wolf Wiki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}